course: dictionary
lesson: 8680
title: Seedlings and young plants
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A seedling is a very young plant that has just grown from a seed. It has its first small leaves, and it needs light, water and care to grow strong.
explain: The ending -ling often means small or young, as in duckling and gosling. So a seedling is a young plant that grew from a seed. Your clues come from the word itself.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The science class grew seedlings from cress on the windowsill» tells you the plants are new and tiny, growing indoors. «Plant out the seedlings» means putting them in the garden once they are big enough.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Water the seedlings every day» still makes sense if you think, water the very young plants every day. If the sentence works, your meaning is probably right.
fact: A seedling is a very young plant that has just grown from a seed.
fact: The ending -ling often means small or young, as in duckling and gosling.
fact: «A bean plant's life cycle is seed, seedling, adult plant with flowers, and pods with new seeds.»
fact: Seedlings need light, water, warmth and soil to grow strong.
fact: «Every Granny Smith tree comes from one seedling found in Australia around 1868.»
exercise: «The science class grew seedlings from cress on the windowsill.» What is a seedling? | A kind of cloud | A fully grown flower with petals | An old tree that has fallen over | *A very young plant that has just grown from a seed
exercise: «Water the seedlings every day and keep them in the light.» What do seedlings need to grow strong? | Sweets and sugar | Darkness and cold | Paint and glue | *Water, light and care
exercise: In «A bean plant's life cycle is seed, seedling, adult plant with flowers, and pods with new seeds», what comes straight after seedling? | A cloud | Mud | *An adult plant with flowers | A seed again
test: «Mountain ash trees need fire to make new seedlings.» What do the trees need fire for? | To keep the forest warm in winter | *To make new seedlings grow | To burn down the forest for good | To turn into flowers
test: Ella says a seedling is a tree with lots of branches. What is the correct meaning? | *A very young plant with its first small leaves | A seed that never grows | A fruit ready to eat | A tree that has been cut down
exam: Which sentence about a seedling is correct? | A seedling is a flower with bright petals | *A seedling is a very young plant with its first small leaves | A seedling is a very old tree with thick bark | A seedling is a seed that never gets wet
